    "title": "Fire inside Two Harbors Lighthouse gift shop causes extensive damage | Local & State News | fox21online.com",
    "text": "TWO HARBORS, Minn. (KQDS-TV) – Days after a fire started inside the Two Harbors Lighthouse gift shop, the Lake County Historical Society said the building needs to be gutted to re-open.\nPictures provided by the Historical Society on Thursday shows the extensive damage inside what's known as the Fog Signal Building.\nThe historic structure was built in 1892.\nThe fire broke out Monday evening.\nCommunity members noticed the flames and called 911.\nNobody was hurt and a cause is under investigation.\nWhile damage estimates are not yet known, the Lake County Historical Society said it's committed to restoring the building and will need financial help doing so.\nDonations can be made in person, through the mail or through the society’s website.",
    "summary": "TWO HARBORS, Minn. (KQDS-TV) – Days after a fire started inside the Two Harbors Lighthouse gift shop, the Lake County Historical Society said the building needs to be gutted to re-open. Pictures provided by the Historical Society on Thursday shows the extensive damage inside what's known as the Fog Signal Building. Community members noticed the flames and called 911. While damage estimates are not yet known, the Lake County Historical Society said it's committed to restoring the building and will need financial help doing so. Donations can be made in person, through the mail or through the society’s website.",
